+**Unreleased table readability correction:** ordinary screen tables prefer
+fitting the article viewport. Technical tokens retain intrinsic word widths;
+exceptionally long tokens can still wrap, and overflow stays in the focusable
+native viewport. For a technical table whose description needs a wider reading
+measure, add `{.td-table--wide}` after the table. This explicit mode keeps the
+max-content policy with a soft `40ch` body-cell measure; it is not a fixed column
+width. The theme does not infer intent from header names, column counts, or code.
+
+`.td-table--wide` selects the inner table's width policy; `.full-width` independently
+selects the available article canvas. Matrix headers keep their existing no-wrap
+behavior. Screen cell sizing is restricted to that table's own rows, and nested
+static viewports reset inherited wrapping. Print/RSS do not acquire wide mode.
+The earlier unconditional-wide proposal is superseded; existing technical
+examples below opt in explicitly. No runtime measurement loop is added.
 
